      "math_academy_id": "q-355207",
      "sequence_position": 9,
      "problem": "Let $T=\\{-2,-1,0,1\\}$ and suppose\n\n$$\ng(-2)=3,\\,g(-1)=-2,\\,g(0)=0,\\,g(1)=-2.\n$$\n\nCompute ${min}_{x\\in T}g(x)$ and $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in T}g(x).$\n\n$\\,$\n${min}_{x\\in T}g(x)=$ {{field-1}}\n\n$\\,$\n$\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in T}g(x)=$ {{field-2}}",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that \n\n- ${min}_{x\\in T}f(x)$ is the smallest output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in T}f(x)$ is an input in $T$ where that smallest output occurs.\n\nThe output values are $3,$ $-2,$ $0,$ and $-2,$ so the minimum output value is $-2.$ This minimum occurs at both $x=-1$ and $x=1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{min}_{x\\in T}g(x)=-2\\,\\text{and}\\,\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in T}g(x)=\\{-1,1\\}.\n$$",
